        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">If you can wall-mount and will use the coaching, buy the Tonal 2</strong>;
            if you cannot drill, or want to keep running costs down, the Speediance Gym Monster 2 is the
            better machine for you. The Tonal 1 Certified Refurbished brings Tonal's training for less
            hardware money but the same membership, the Voltra I makes a power rack smart without a
            subscription, and Tempo Move is the small, cheap way to get coached dumbbell training.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, price it over three years with the membership included, check the wall or
            floor before ordering, and keep a plan for the heavy lifts that 200 or 250 lb of cable cannot
            cover. If a coach on the wall is less important than a cable station that never needs a fee,
